    "notes": "Built on the door-arrivals winner (KG-2026-10-27-c, skip 25.6%, watched 72%): same doorbell rhythm, one guest per ring, a count chip that climbs, host undone by her own rule and the opening line thrown back at her. The game plays three times: Ruhi ordinary (one message), Avika sillier (telling someone she is 5 minutes away while standing at the door, her catchphrase), Zoya absurd (claims 'Done!' happily, then two more phones). Twist is see-and-hear: three dings and a phone popping at Tanya's pallu, no reasoning needed. Ruhi stays silent until the chorus so only Tanya, Avika and Zoya talk. Rewrite 1: the first ending had Tanya hiding the call and walking off; weaker than the mirrored entry line. Endings tried: guests lock Tanya out (unkind for her own house), Tanya's son calls to ask where the remote is (needs a voice we do not have), chorus line back at her (kept). Pace 28 because the last QA failure was pace."
